# 5.3 Mathematical Formulation

Suppose there are

\[
n
\]

cities.

The distances between cities are represented by

\[
d_{ij}
\]

where

\[
d_{ij}
\]

denotes the distance from city

\[
i
\]

to city

\[
j.
\]

The objective function becomes

\[
\min \sum d_{ij}x_{ij}
\]

where

- \(x_{ij}=1\) if the route travels from city \(i\) to city \(j\),
- otherwise \(x_{ij}=0\).

The optimization is performed while satisfying the constraints that each city has exactly one incoming edge and one outgoing edge.

This mathematical formulation forms the foundation for later conversion into a **QUBO model**.

