# 5.6 Real-World Applications

Despite its theoretical origin,

the Travelling Salesman Problem appears in numerous practical applications.

### Logistics

Companies such as DHL, UPS, Amazon, and FedEx must determine efficient delivery routes while minimizing transportation costs.

---

### Railway Transportation

Rail operators, including Deutsche Bahn, optimize train scheduling, maintenance planning, and routing problems that resemble large TSP instances.

---

### Airline Scheduling

Airlines optimize aircraft rotations, crew assignments, and airport scheduling.

---

### Manufacturing

Factories determine the optimal order for machining operations and robotic assembly paths.

---

### Warehouse Automation

Autonomous robots must determine efficient paths while collecting products from multiple storage locations.

---

### Healthcare

Hospitals optimize ambulance routing, home healthcare visits, and laboratory sample transportation.

These examples demonstrate that TSP is far more than an academic exercise—it is a fundamental industrial optimization problem.

